
## --help → the usage
rc=0
.what = prove a clamp BITES: revert the fix to HEAD, run the play (it must
        fail a claim), restore the fix, run it again (it must pass)

.why  = `rule.require.clamp-edge-cases` owes this for every defect fix — a
        clamp that stays green with the fix reverted exercises no defect.
        by hand it is a backup, N reverts, two runs, and N restores, and a
        restore missed by hand leaves the fix silently gone from the tree

usage:
  rhx play.clamp.verify --play <slug> --revert <path> [--revert <path> …]
  rhx play.clamp.verify --play prove.carried-tree-serves-reach \
    --revert src/grove.provision/5.devtools/5.13.reach/_.sh

options:
  --play SLUG    a tracked play under `.play/permanent/` (as `play.run`)
  --revert PATH  a tracked file whose fix to set aside; repeat per file.
                 each must DIFFER from HEAD, else the revert proves naught
  --within SECS  bound per run, passed to `play.run` (default 900)
  -h, --help     show this header

guarantee:
  - every reverted file is restored on ANY exit (a trap), then compared byte
    for byte to its backup; a mismatch is a malfunction, named per file
  - the red run must fail a CLAIM (exit 1). a decline (exit 2) bites no defect
  - it writes only the named files, and only to their HEAD content and back

exit:
  0 = red with the fix reverted, green with it restored
  1 = the clamp did not bite, did not go green, or a restore failed
  2 = a constraint: bad args, an untracked path, or a path equal to HEAD

## an unknown option → refused, names the valid
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: unknown option '--every'
   └─ valid: --play <slug>  --revert <path> (repeat)  --within <secs>  --help

## no --play → refused
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: --play is required

## no --revert → refused
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: at least one --revert is required

## an untracked path → refused
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: 'untracked.txt' is not tracked, so it has no HEAD to revert to

## a path equal to HEAD → refused
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: 'still.txt' equals HEAD — there is no fix in it to revert
   └─ ⇒ name only the files that carry the fix

## a path staged new, absent from HEAD → refused
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: 'stagednew.txt' is new on this branch, so HEAD holds no prior version to revert to
   └─ ⇒ name the file that CALLS it (that one has a HEAD), or remove the one guard line by hand

## outside a git checkout → refused
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: not inside a git checkout

## a clamp that bites → red, then green
rc=0
🐢 lets see if it bites

🐚 play.clamp.verify --play prove.subject-is-fixed
   ├─ reverted to HEAD
   │  ├─ subject.txt
   │  └─ (1 file(s))
   ├─ fix reverted → exit 1 · 1 claim(s) failed
   │  ✋ subject.txt is not fixed
   └─ fix restored → exit 0 · 0 claim(s) failed

🌊 righteous — red without the fix, green with it

## a clamp green both ways → did not bite
rc=1
🐢 lets see if it bites

🐚 play.clamp.verify --play prove.always-holds
   ├─ reverted to HEAD
   │  ├─ other.txt
   │  └─ (1 file(s))
   ├─ fix reverted → exit 0 · 0 claim(s) failed
   └─ fix restored → exit 0 · 0 claim(s) failed

💥 MalfunctionError: the clamp did not bite: exit 0 with the fix reverted, where a failed claim is exit 1
   └─ ⇒ every claim held without the fix: rewrite the clamp to exercise the defect

## a play that declines → a decline, never a bite
rc=1
🐢 lets see if it bites

🐚 play.clamp.verify --play prove.always-declines
   ├─ reverted to HEAD
   │  ├─ other.txt
   │  └─ (1 file(s))
   ├─ fix reverted → exit 2 · 0 claim(s) failed
   │  ✋ ConstraintError: prove.always-declines declined — its subject is absent, so it proved no claim
   └─ fix restored → exit 2 · 0 claim(s) failed

💥 MalfunctionError: the clamp did not bite: exit 2 with the fix reverted, where a failed claim is exit 1
   └─ ⇒ exit 2 is a decline — the play could not run, so it proved no claim

## a clamp red both ways → not green
rc=1
🐢 lets see if it bites

🐚 play.clamp.verify --play prove.always-fails
   ├─ reverted to HEAD
   │  ├─ other.txt
   │  └─ (1 file(s))
   ├─ fix reverted → exit 1 · 1 claim(s) failed
   │  💥 MalfunctionError: a claim the fix does not touch
   └─ fix restored → exit 1 · 1 claim(s) failed

💥 MalfunctionError: the clamp is not green with the fix restored (exit 1)
   └─ 💥 MalfunctionError: a claim the fix does not touch

## a play that crashes on revert → no bite
rc=1
🐢 lets see if it bites

🐚 play.clamp.verify --play prove.crashes-on-revert
   ├─ reverted to HEAD
   │  ├─ subject.txt
   │  └─ (1 file(s))
   ├─ fix reverted → exit 1 · 0 claim(s) failed
   └─ fix restored → exit 0 · 0 claim(s) failed

💥 MalfunctionError: the clamp did not bite: exit 1 with the fix reverted, and no claim failed
   └─ ⇒ the play crashed rather than caught the defect; its last lines:
      ⇒ it said: 🎭 play.run --play prove.crashes-on-revert --within 30
      ⇒ it said: <fixture>/repo/.play/permanent/prove.crashes-on-revert.play.sh
      ⇒ it said: line 3: an_absent_function: command not found
      ⇒ it said: 💥 MalfunctionError: prove.crashes-on-revert failed (exit 1)

